#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Seed the knobas XWiki test instance over its REST API.

    testenv/seed            create whatever is missing (re-run creates nothing)
    testenv/seed --verify   read a few things back; exit 1 if any is missing

Every write is preceded by a read: a user, page, comment, tag set or attachment
that is already there is left alone. Pages are written by the fixture person
who authored them (basic auth as that user), so `author`/`creator` are real
XWiki users. Page dates are seed time: XWiki's REST API cannot backdate a page.
Comment dates come from the fixture (an XWikiComments object's `date` is an
ordinary property).

Environment: XWIKI_URL (default http://127.0.0.1:8099/xwiki, the tunnel),
XWIKI_SUPERADMIN_PASSWORD (default knobas-superadmin).
"""

